---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Connections and environments — Querial">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-querial-sky">For DevOps</p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mt-1">Connections and environments</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 [&>p]:text-muted-foreground [&>h2]:text-foreground">
            <p>
                A <strong class="text-foreground">logical connection</strong> has a name and a
                provider. It is not an environment catalog row. EnvironmentKind is a closed
                enum: development, staging, production. Each kind has its own encrypted
                endpoint (host, credentials, command timeout, connect timeout). Runtime
                resolves <code class="text-foreground">(connection_id, kind) → endpoint</code>.
            </p>
            <p>
                Steps store the logical connection. Monaco dialect follows that provider.
                There is no pipeline-level supported-providers gate and no per-step
                connection remap at deploy time.
            </p>

            <h2>Who can test and edit</h2>
            <p>
                Test and edit endpoints are operator actions (CanOperate). Developers
                never hit non-development secrets via Test. After a breaking cutover that
                wipes legacy secrets, operators re-enter per-kind secrets — they are not
                copied.
            </p>

            <h2>SQL against kinds</h2>
            <p>
                You may preview and refresh schema against any kind. Production SQL is
                still interactive, not a pipeline run. Command timeout on the endpoint is
                one of three clocks (with lease/grace and cancel); it is snapshotted onto
                executions when a run is planned.
            </p>

            <h2>Optional default on a deployment</h2>
            <p>
                <code class="text-foreground">deployments.connection_id</code> is an optional
                default logical connection used only by legacy published steps that still
                have a null connection. New publishes require every step and migration bound.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
